inds fade, or if macroeconomic conditions worsen. A conservative approach doesn’t mean missing out on opportunities—it means protecting capital and ensuring that any exposure is well-calibrated to the firm’s risk tolerance.  In the end, the Risky Analyst is betting on the assumption that the current momentum will continue indefinitely. That’s a dangerous assumption. A low-risk strategy isn’t about avoiding all risk—it’s about making sure that any risk taken is measured, understood, and aligned with the firm’s long-term goals.
